Tulepaak OÜ is a specialist consultancy and software development company focused on designing, building, and modernising government registry solutions, with a particular emphasis on business registries and foundational digital government platforms. Drawing on more than 20 years of hands-on experience with complex e-government initiatives, Tulepaak’s experts have played a central role in the design, implementation, and continuous evolution of Estonia’s e-Business Register and broader e-transformation, helping to turn Estonia into one of the world’s most advanced digital states.
The company combines deep domain knowledge in legal entity registration, interoperability, and regulatory compliance with a product-led, user-centric delivery model. From discovery through to design, implementation, and change management, Tulepaak works closely with public-sector clients to simplify user journeys, automate back-office workflows, and ensure legislative agility through modular, scalable architectures. Its teams have successfully delivered high-impact programs in Europe and the Middle East, including fully digital business registry management systems, XBRL-based annual reporting solutions, single-window self-service portals, and cross-border interoperability projects (such as BRIS, cross-border e-signature, and X-Road based data exchange).
Tulepaak increasingly integrates advanced AI capabilities into registry and government workflows, applying AI for process automation, intelligent validation, document understanding, and decision support, so that routine and judgement-based tasks are handled faster and with fewer errors. Leveraging modern “vibe coding” practices—where developers and domain experts describe desired behaviour in natural language and AI systems generate and refine the underlying code—Tulepaak accelerates prototyping and delivery while keeping architecture, security, and governance under expert control. This allows public-sector clients to experiment rapidly, iterate on services, and embed AI into core business processes without compromising robustness or compliance.
Tulepaak’s capabilities span solution architecture, business and service design, AI-assisted software engineering, interoperability and API design, data exchange, and organisational change management. Typical engagements involve small, senior, agile teams—led by experienced delivery and change managers—who work in close partnership with client organisations to reduce risk while maximising knowledge transfer and long-term sustainability. Through this approach, Tulepaak consistently delivers smart, sustainable, and future-proof registry solutions that enhance transparency, efficiency, and user trust in government services, while progressively embedding AI as a native component of digital-era public administration.
